{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder\/batchLimit"},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"batchLimit","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/PropertyJSON\/documentation\/PropertyJSON\/BatchLimit","preciseIdentifier":"s:12PropertyJSON10BatchLimitV","text":"BatchLimit","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Snowplow’s mobile trackers send at most 25 events and 40,000 bytes in a request by default,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and an event larger than that in a request of its own. A collector refuses a body over 2 MB"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with 413, and a request larger than its stream takes (192,000 bytes on SQS, 1 MB on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Kinesis, by default) becomes a failed event though the collector answers 200. So an event"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of up to 150,000 bytes of JSON is sent alone, within the smallest of those, and a larger one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is left out as "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowEncodingError\/oversized(byteCount:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/snowplowencoding\/snowplowbatchencoder\/batchlimit"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"title":"batchLimit","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"SnowplowEncoding"}],"fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"batchLimit","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BatchLimit","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12PropertyJSON10BatchLimitV"}],"roleHeading":"Type Property","symbolKind":"property","remoteSource":{"fileName":"SnowplowBatchEncoder.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder.swift#L122"},"externalID":"s:16SnowplowEncoding0A12BatchEncoderV10batchLimit12PropertyJSON0cF0VvpZ"},"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding","doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Snowplow’s trackers’ limits on one request, 25 events and 40,000 bytes of body, and an event"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of up to 150,000 bytes in a request of its own."}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"references":{"doc://PropertyJSON/documentation/PropertyJSON/BatchLimit":{"url":"\/documentation\/propertyjson\/batchlimit","abstract":[{"text":"The most an ingestion endpoint takes in one request: how many records, how many bytes of body,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and how many bytes of one record’s JSON.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"BatchLimit","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/PropertyJSON\/documentation\/PropertyJSON\/BatchLimit","title":"BatchLimit","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BatchLimit","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://SnowplowEncoding/documentation/SnowplowEncoding":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/snowplowencoding","abstract":[{"text":"Send records to a Snowplow collector as self-describing events, whose schemas come from the tracking plan.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"d